  [3mError handling[0m
  - [1mBroken stored data:[0m [38;5;153mgetSession()[39m wraps [38;5;153mJSON.parse[39m in try/catch. If the stored value is broken or isn't the expected
    shape (no [38;5;153muserId[39m), it returns [38;5;153mnull[39m and removes the bad key, so the app recovers by itself instead of failing on
    every page.
  - [1mlocalStorage unavailable[0m (some private-browsing modes, storage turned off, quota full): [38;5;153msetSession[39m and [38;5;153mclearSession[39m
    catch the error and log a [38;5;153mconsole.warn[39m, and the login still succeeds. You just aren't remembered after a reload.
    [38;5;153mgetSession[39m returns [38;5;153mnull[39m in that case.
  - [1mFailed login:[0m nothing is saved. Any existing session stays as it is; that's for a future logout or re-login to
    handle.

